Notes (so you don’t get surprised in prod)

These updates do not reuse a different active_job_id when /run returns already_running for a different run. That’s intentional: it preserves your existing cross-run queueing semantics.

If you later want “reattach to active_job_id even if job_id differs” (stronger de-dup across new runs), tell me — I’ll add a reattach_policy switch.

If you want, I can also package these into two updated .py files in your sandbox paths so you can drop-in replace them directly.
